Proposed minimal fix to resolve the heap-use-after-free in div_function when the destination (result) is the same as the dividend (op1).

Root cause (summary): In div_function, when handling division with potential failure, the code destructs the destination zval (result) before performing a second division attempt using div_function_base. If the operation then fails (e.g., division by zero) and subsequent bytecode handlers access the freed zval, a heap-use-after-free can occur. The fix is to avoid destroying the destination zval early and compute into a temporary zval first, then copy back to result on success.

Patch (minimal, two hunks):
--- a/Zend/zend_operators.c
+++ b/Zend/zend_operators.c
@@
-    if (result == op1) {
-        zval_ptr_dtor(result);
-    }
+    // Do not destroy the destination zval here to avoid heap-use-after-free
+    // in self-division scenarios. We will compute into a temporary and only
+    // copy back on success.
@@
-    retval = div_function_base(result, &op1_copy, &op2_copy);
+    zval tmp_res;
+    ZVAL_UNDEF(&tmp_res);
+    retval = div_function_base(&tmp_res, &op1_copy, &op2_copy);
     if (retval == SUCCESS) {
-        return SUCCESS;
+        ZVAL_COPY_VALUE(result, &tmp_res);
+        return SUCCESS;
     }
*** End Patch

